WEBVTT

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.392
Mavis, honey, are you all right?

00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:12.562
Yeah, I think so. That was weird.

00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:14.564
My head hurts.

00:00:14.689 --> 00:00:16.566
-Who is that?
-Who is what?

00:00:16.691 --> 00:00:18.235
Oh, that.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.237
That is nobody.

00:00:20.362 --> 00:00:22.114
-Seriously, Dad?
-"Dad"?

00:00:22.239 --> 00:00:26.034
Yeah, I know, Dracula's daughter.
Everyone freaks out at first.

00:00:26.076 --> 00:00:27.244
Dracula?

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.411
Okay, we got to go.

00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:34.084
Please don't kill me. I'm so young.

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:36.545
I have so many places I want to see.

00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:38.880
I've got tickets to six
Dave Matthews Band concerts.

00:00:38.922 --> 00:00:40.799
I'm getting out of here.

00:00:44.094 --> 00:00:45.470
Shut up already.

00:00:45.595 --> 00:00:48.098
It's impossible for me
to think with all your noise.

00:00:48.223 --> 00:00:50.433
Sorry, Glen. Go back to sleep.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:56.606
-Wait. Aren't you going to suck my blood?
-Classic human paranoia.

00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:00.652
Human blood is so fatty,
and you never know where it's been.

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:03.488
So, Dracula doesn't drink blood?

00:01:03.613 --> 00:01:05.991
No, I use a blood substitute.

00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:10.412
Either Near Blood or Blood Beaters.
You can't tell the difference.

00:01:10.453 --> 00:01:13.290
So, wow, you're, like, the real Count Dracula.

00:01:13.415 --> 00:01:16.126
Like, "I'm Dracula. Bleh, bleh-bleh."

00:01:16.793 --> 00:01:19.880
I've never said that in my life.
"Bleh, bleh-bleh."

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:21.631
I don't know where that comes from.

00:01:21.756 --> 00:01:25.135
Can I just ask, what exactly is this place?

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.637
What is this place?

00:01:31.516 --> 00:01:35.604
It's a place I built
for all those monsters out there,

00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:40.984
lurking in the shadows,
hiding from the persecution of humankind.

00:01:41.151 --> 00:01:45.572
A place for them and their families
to come to and be themselves.

00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:49.075
A place void of torches,
pitchforks, angry mobs.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:52.412
A place of peace, relaxation

00:01:52.495 --> 00:01:54.664
and tranquility.

00:01:54.831 --> 00:01:56.917
Cool. So, it's like a hotel for monsters?

00:01:57.959 --> 00:02:01.838
Yes, exactly. "A hotel for monsters."
Way to sum it up.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:06.384
Okay, hop on my back. We're leaving.

00:02:06.468 --> 00:02:08.094
Oh, man, you're a bat now.

00:02:08.178 --> 00:02:10.013
I always wanted to fly. What's it like?

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:13.266
This is insane. Wait. Wait, I want to stay.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.894
Can Frankenstein sign my costume?
Can I meet the Invisible Man?

00:02:15.977 --> 00:02:18.438
Hey, if I stuck my hand
in the Invisible Man's mouth,

00:02:18.521 --> 00:02:20.106
-would it disappear?
-Hi.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.069
Mavey! What are you doing,
my sweet little blood orange?

00:02:24.152 --> 00:02:26.196
Our friend was just leaving.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.240
Yeah, he was flying me out the window.

00:02:29.491 --> 00:02:30.867
This guy, he's so funny.

00:02:31.034 --> 00:02:33.495
Look, you have something on your face.

00:02:33.536 --> 00:02:37.332
Play along if you ever want
to see your precious backpack.

00:02:40.043 --> 00:02:43.964
Whoa. So, wait, you didn't have
any clothes on when you were a bat?

00:02:44.047 --> 00:02:45.340
Or were they bat-sized?

00:02:46.258 --> 00:02:48.385
Who exactly is that?

00:02:48.551 --> 00:02:49.886
Honeybat.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.180
You see, it's your birthday.

00:02:52.222 --> 00:02:57.060
And you know I want you to have the bestest,
specialest party of your life.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.397
So, well, I needed some help.

00:03:00.522 --> 00:03:01.731
You needed help?

00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:05.235
Well, look, I am very good,
but I thought it would be

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:10.699
even more bestest, specialest if someone
closer to your age helped plan the party.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.033
-You're my age?
-Sure.

00:03:12.075 --> 00:03:13.743
Well, how old are you?

00:03:13.827 --> 00:03:14.911
118.

00:03:14.995 --> 00:03:16.746
One hundred and...

00:03:16.871 --> 00:03:19.666
Yeah, I'm 121.

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:21.543
Really?

00:03:21.584 --> 00:03:25.380
You see? Everything is very, very normal.

00:03:25.422 --> 00:03:28.216
I'm throwing a party, and he's helping.

00:03:28.425 --> 00:03:30.468
-Sir, there's an emergency.
-Not now.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.264
Can't you see we're in the middle
of something very normal here?

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.890
Wait, what's going on here?

00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:40.228
There's an emergency in your precious hotel,
and you're not running to fix it?

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.896
Why? Is it because of him?

00:03:41.938 --> 00:03:43.773
Whoa, look at my face.

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:47.777
No, precious bones, it's not because of him.

00:03:47.902 --> 00:03:50.739
Good. Then go check on the emergency,
and I'll keep him company.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.742
-No! Anything but that!
-What?

00:03:53.783 --> 00:03:56.536
I mean, because he needs time to plan.

00:03:56.619 --> 00:03:59.456
And if you're keeping him company,
then he's not planning.

00:03:59.581 --> 00:04:01.374
He is company-keeping,

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:03.793
and then the plan, it's...
It doesn't get planned.

00:04:04.794 --> 00:04:06.254
-Good one.
-Shut up!

00:04:06.296 --> 00:04:10.425
Okay. So, maybe if you're not
planning later, we can hang out.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.053
-Sounds good.
-Yes. You hear that?

00:04:13.136 --> 00:04:14.679
It sounds good.

00:04:14.971 --> 00:04:18.850
So you will hang out.
See you later, my honey. Lovely.

00:04:19.642 --> 00:04:21.478
Okay, you're not hanging out.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.480
Because you are leaving.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.607
But the opposite, you said.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.820
But, sir, the emergency.

00:04:30.904 --> 00:04:32.405
Follow me.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.162
Boy, that kid smelled.

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:44.751
Where are we going?

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.169
Just getting rid of you

00:04:46.294 --> 00:04:49.005
through a secret tunnel
so she does not see us.

00:04:49.172 --> 00:04:51.383
So, can I ask you a question?

00:04:51.508 --> 00:04:53.635
Is that real, about the garlic thing?

00:04:53.802 --> 00:04:56.763
Yes, I cannot have it. My throat swells.

00:04:57.013 --> 00:04:58.681
Wooden stake to the heart?

00:04:58.723 --> 00:05:00.392
Yeah, well, who wouldn't that kill?

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.986
Here we go.

00:05:15.824 --> 00:05:17.575
I'm sorry. I'm a little lost.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.203
Yes, I know it's your honeymoon.
I apologize.

00:05:20.245 --> 00:05:23.164
Go back to doing what you were doing.

00:05:27.836 --> 00:05:29.045
I'm not down here much.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:32.715
It's meant to be
an exit if humans ever invade.

00:05:32.841 --> 00:05:36.636
So, I'm, like, the first human here, huh?
That's really cool.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.139
Oh, boy.

00:05:39.222 --> 00:05:41.224
I think this is it.

00:05:44.144 --> 00:05:45.895
-What's happening?
-I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.398
-My mistake.
-What is wrong with you people?

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.361
Oh, man. This place is amazing.

00:05:53.403 --> 00:05:55.780
Okay, I could really use
some silence right now.

00:06:02.912 --> 00:06:04.914
All right, third time's a...

00:06:11.921 --> 00:06:13.256
Drac.

00:06:13.923 --> 00:06:15.175
Yes, Frankie?

00:06:15.258 --> 00:06:16.551
Hey, buddy, what you been doing?

00:06:16.593 --> 00:06:17.844
Don't move.

00:06:17.927 --> 00:06:19.679
Never mind that. What you been doing?

00:06:20.263 --> 00:06:22.682
We wanted to practice our
big number for Mavis's party,

00:06:22.765 --> 00:06:24.851
and then these losers
wouldn't get off the bandstand.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.603
Okay. Put down Zombie Mozart,

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:28.271
Bach and Beethoven this instant.

00:06:32.442 --> 00:06:35.778
Did you get to rehearse
at all, Zombie Beethoven?

00:06:37.614 --> 00:06:41.451
Listen, Drac, we wanted to
play something, like old times.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.953
We even thought maybe you'd sing with us.

00:06:44.037 --> 00:06:48.291
Come on, fellas. You know that
I haven't sung in public since Martha.

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:50.668
Yeah, but we just thought
how much, you know, Mavis would love it.

00:06:50.752 --> 00:06:51.794
I said no!

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.046
Don't ask me again!

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.633
Okay. Now, let's hug the zombies.
Let's all make up.

00:06:56.758 --> 00:06:59.302
-Wow. He really scared you.
-I wasn't scared.

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:01.304
I was being polite, okay?

00:07:01.596 --> 00:07:04.557
Hey. What are you doing here?
I thought you were planning.

00:07:04.641 --> 00:07:07.060
I never caught your name.

00:07:07.143 --> 00:07:08.228
My name's Mavis.

00:07:08.478 --> 00:07:10.980
Mavis? That's a pretty neat name.

00:07:11.064 --> 00:07:12.649
Yeah, my mom picked it.

00:07:12.815 --> 00:07:15.985
So, are you going to tell me your name?

00:07:16.069 --> 00:07:20.073
Me? My name? Good question.

00:07:20.156 --> 00:07:22.075
Well, obviously, I'm Frankenstein.

00:07:22.867 --> 00:07:24.827
No, you're not.
Frankenstein is my uncle over there.

00:07:25.286 --> 00:07:26.871
The gentleman hugging Zombie Mozart.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.458
Right. Of course, he's your uncle.

00:07:30.542 --> 00:07:33.670
Well, see, I'm not "the" Frankenstein.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:37.382
I'm his cousin, Johnnystein.

00:07:37.465 --> 00:07:39.717
-Johnnystein?
-Hey, Mavis.

00:07:42.762 --> 00:07:45.223
Who is that?

00:07:45.306 --> 00:07:46.724
Are these monsters going to kill me?

00:07:46.808 --> 00:07:48.893
Not as long as they think you're a monster.

00:07:48.977 --> 00:07:50.395
Huh? That's kind of racist.

00:07:50.478 --> 00:07:51.938
We'll talk later.

